                <pb facs="0596" n="478" sameAs="frus:frus1928v02/pg478"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.9331/71: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >MacMurray</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1928-07-27T10:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">July 27,
                                1928—10 a.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received July 27—1:45
                    a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>574. Your No. 240, July 26, 9 a.m. just received. Regret it is too late to change
                    arrangements made with Chinese who I understand have already left. The fact of
                    signature of treaty has also leaked out.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">MacMurray</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
